## Bug Report

### Version

`next-openapi-gen@1.10.0` (also 1.7.3)

### Description

A `z.discriminatedUnion` whose variants are named schemas gets a `discriminator` without a `mapping`.

`processZodDiscriminatedUnion` means to map each `$ref` variant to its literal ("When the variant is emitted as `$ref`, point the mapping entry at the ref"), but it reads the literal from `variant.properties`. A `$ref` has no properties of its own, so no literal is found and the mapping stays empty.

Without a `mapping`, OpenAPI's implicit discriminator values are the component *names* (`circleSchema`, `squareSchema`), not the literals (`circle`, `square`). Clients that follow the spec key the union on those names. For example, `@hey-api/openapi-ts` generates `({ kind: 'circleSchema' } & CircleSchema) | …`, which collapses to `never` against `kind: 'circle'`, so the request body can't be typed.

### Minimal Reproduction

```ts
// src/schemas/shapes.ts
import { z } from "zod";

export const circleSchema = z.object({ kind: z.literal("circle"), radius: z.number() });
export const squareSchema = z.object({ kind: z.literal("square"), side: z.number() });
export const shapeSchema = z.discriminatedUnion("kind", [circleSchema, squareSchema]);
```

```ts
// src/app/api/shapes/route.ts
/**
 * Create a shape
 * @body shapeSchema
 * @response shapeSchema
 * @openapi
 */
export async function POST() {
  return Response.json({});
}
```

### Actual Output

```json
"shapeSchema": {
  "type": "object",
  "discriminator": { "propertyName": "kind" },
  "oneOf": [
    { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/circleSchema" },
    { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/squareSchema" }
  ]
}
```

### Expected Output

```json
"shapeSchema": {
  "type": "object",
  "discriminator": {
    "propertyName": "kind",
    "mapping": {
      "circle": "#/components/schemas/circleSchema",
      "square": "#/components/schemas/squareSchema"
    }
  },
  "oneOf": [
    { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/circleSchema" },
    { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/squareSchema" }
  ]
}
```

### Suggested fix

When a variant is a `$ref`, read the literal from the component it points to. The converter's `zodSchemas` is keyed by component name, so a lookup by the `$ref`'s name also covers `.meta({ id })` renames and `…Output` components.

I have a PR ready with the fix and a test. The existing unit test for the mapping passes a `$ref` that also carries `properties`, which real output never does, so it doesn't catch this.
